## Original Content
Archeologists are confronting an “unfathomable” loss as border wall construction is set to cut across ranches that are home to unique historical sites, many of which haven’t been fully studied.

## Summary
Border wall construction is set to destroy private ranches that house unique archeological sites dating back 6,000 years. Many of these sites have not been fully studied, and archeologists fear an irreversible loss of historical knowledge.

## Key Points
- Border wall construction threatens ancient archeological sites on private lands.
- The sites span 6,000 years of history and have not been fully excavated or researched.
- Archeologists are confronting a significant and potentially irreversible loss of historical data.


